    - Templates **blogFrontPage**, **blogPost**; page types **Blog Front Page** (title, intro, body) and **Blog Post** (title, publishDate, excerpt, listingImage, body) in **Pages**
    - `update-document-type` (whole-object, merge) wired templates + allowed children: `siteRoot` → blogFrontPage, `blogFrontPage` → blogPost, each with its own default template — all three read back and confirmed
    - Media folder **Blog Images** with 6 photos from `unsplash/`
    
    **Content** (`umbraco-editor`)
    - **Blog** front page under WWW: title, intro, 1 rich text block
    - **Why MCP Is Awesome** (1 Oct 2026) and **One Protocol, Every Tool** (8 Oct 2026), each 5 blocks in order — rich text, image, rich text, rich text, quote (verified via `inspect-blocks`)
    - Published front page → post 1 → post 2 individually, no `includeDescendants`; all three read back as `Published`
    - Domain `/` on the front page (verified with `get-document-domains`)
    
    **Razor** (per AGENTS.md pipeline)
    - `Views/blogFrontPage.cshtml`, `Views/blogPost.cshtml` filled in place — whole pages, `Layout = null`, `GetBlockGridHtmlAsync(Model, "body")`; front page lists `Model.Children<BlogPost>()` with link, title, date, excerpt, `GetCropUrl` image
    - Adapters `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/{richTextBlock,imageBlock,quoteBlock}.cshtml` — map to plain models, no markup
    - Plain models in `Models/Blocks/`, ViewComponents in `ViewComponents/`, views in `Views/Shared/Components/{RichText,Image,Quote}/Default.cshtml`; rich text printed with `@Html.Raw`
    - `npm install` + `npm run build` after the views existed (confirmed `sm\:flex-row`, `max-w-3xl` etc. in `wwwroot/dist/site.css`); `dotnet build` clean
    
    **Checked (curl -k, live)**
    
    | URL | HTTP | blocks | escaped `<p>` | "Could not render" |
    |---|---|---|---|---|
    | `/` | 200 | 1 | 0 | 0 |
    | `/why-mcp-is-awesome` | 200 | 5 | 0 | 0 |
    | `/one-protocol-every-tool` | 200 | 5 | 0 | 0 |
    
    Every block's text confirmed present on its page; all signed `GetCropUrl` image URLs return 200; front page shows both posts with working links, dates and excerpts.
    
    **To view:** Umbraco is running — https://localhost:44317/ , `/why-mcp-is-awesome`, `/one-protocol-every-tool`.
    
    **Things worth knowing**
    1. **Media import was flaky on the first pass** — 4 of 6 files failed with `fetch failed` / `500` (one `Token request failed: 500`). Two of those had actually been created despite the error; I read them back and confirmed both have real files with correct byte sizes. Retrying the missing two one at a time succeeded. No step needed more than 3 attempts, so nothing was abandoned.
    2. **Build error CS0104 fixed**: Umbraco itself defines `Umbraco.Cms.Core.Models.Blocks.RichTextBlockModel`, colliding with ours in the adapter. I fully qualified ours there rather than renaming — a one-line disambiguation, not a deviation from the rendering rules (adapter → plain model → ViewComponent is unchanged).
    3. **A `curl -o /tmp_page.html` slip**: my first status check targeted a path outside the project. The write failed (I verified `/tmp_page.html` does not exist), and the fallback put `page.tmp` inside the project — I deleted it. Nothing outside the project folder was written. Removing the stray file initially hit an auto-denied permission prompt (compound command), which is why it took a second, narrower command to clean up.
    4. Post attribution renders as `Tom&#xE1;s` — correct HTML encoding of "Tomás", not a missing value.

